  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2ee87e681215b6147a44021cf30db039, type: 3}
  m_Name: 4.Grandmaster's palace entrance
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  nameOfPoint: "Grandmaster\u2019s palace entrance on Archbishop\u2019s Street"
  coordinatesPoint: {x: 14.51404, y: 35.8996}
  firstPartInfo: 'When Malta became a British colony in 1800, the palace of the Grandmasters
    of the Knights of St John became the seat of the colonial governor. In this building,
    all the power of the colonial state was concentrated - at the time, the building
    also housed the police headquarters. When he was brought to Valletta by boat,
    it is here that Isidoro Mifsud was taken to be questioned by Sgt Major Giovanni
    Scicluna, and for his case to undergo the procedure of inquiry towards a formal
    charge. The police obtained the testimonies of the Grech family members and other
    people who knew the family and the accused, regarding the burglary, and built
    up a case file.  How many others must he have brushed shoulders with, who were
    driven to break the law out of desperation? '
  secondPartInfo: 'What consequences would Isidoro Mifsud have been facing for his
    crime? The prospect of imprisonment or forced labour was hard. Yet, he would
    not be the only one who might have felt the weight of punishment. There were
    other consequences, felt by the family of the convicted - especially if that
    family was poor.  Apart from the accused being brought to the police station,
    this building would also have seen another steady stream of arrivals: individuals
    who wished to petition the governor, in the hope of their plea reaching the ear
    of someone with the power to help. In some cases, these individuals would have
    been pleading for the release of a family member from prison.  Where would these
    individuals have entered the city? Through the same gate that most people arrive
    in Valletta to this day - that is where I shall head next. '
  imgMarker: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c98feaebd40d8df449e6d3855ac84352, type: 3}
  imgMain: {fileID: 21300000, guid: f26fa8880b3aeef4b8516c82dc12f2a5, type: 3}
  nameOfStory: Poverty
  hintOfPOI: "It\u2019s one of my favourite places to roam! It\u2019s a great place
    to beg for treats from all the people just getting off the bus and walking into
    Valletta. I also love to weave through the feet of the politicians walking into
    Parliament and try to trip them up!"
  solutionOfPOI: Where does one enter the city from? City Gate, of course!
